x satisfying version from available[constraint.name].\n  If no versions available for a name, skip it (don't include in results).\n  If versions available but none satisfy the range, skip it.\nFor satisfies(): use semver.satisfies(version, range)\nFor maxSatisfying(): use semver.maxSatisfying(versions, range) — returns null if none satisfy\nFor validRange(): use semver.validRange(range) !== null\n\nWrite the complete implementation to /workspace/src/resolver/index.ts using the Write tool.`, { label: 'resolver' }),\n\n  () => agent(`Write /workspace/src/runner/index.ts — the Sandboxed Runner module.\n\nProject context:\n- TypeScript ESM project (type: module, Node16 module resolution)\n- Use Node.js built-in vm module (NOT vm2)\n- Types are in src/types.ts (DO NOT modify)\n- Import types with: import type { SandboxResult, RunnerService } from '../types.js';\n- Import vm with: import vm from 'node:vm';\n\nImplement and export a createRunner() function that returns a RunnerService object.\n\nThe RunnerService interface (from types.ts) is:\n  execute(code: string, context?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<SandboxResult>;\n  executeWithTimeout(code: string, timeoutMs: number, context?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<SandboxResult>;\n\nSandboxResult is: { success: boolean; output: unknown; duration: number; memoryUsed: number; error?: string }\n\nImplementation approach:\n1. execute() should call executeWithTimeout() with a default timeout of 5000ms\n2. Core execution logic:\n   a. Record start time with Date.now() and initial memory with process.memoryUsage().heapUsed\n   b. Create a sandbox object with:\n      - Spread the context variables (if any)\n      - A custom console: { log, error, warn } that appends to a captured output array\n      - module: { exports: {} as unknown } for CommonJS-style exports\n      - exports: pointing to module.exports\n   c. Wrap the user code: \"(function(module, exports, console) { \" + code + \" })(module, exports, console)\"\n   d. Create a vm.Script with the wrapped code\n   e. Create a vm context with vm.createContext(sandbox)\n   f. Call script.runInContext(ctx, { timeout: timeoutMs })\n   g. Record end time and memory\n   h. Return SandboxResult with success=true, output=captured console output array (if any logs) else module.exports value, duration, memoryUsed\n3. On error (including timeout which throws with message \"Script execution timed out\"):\n   - Return SandboxResult with success=false, output=null, error=err.message, duration, memoryUsed\n\nIMPORTANT: The timeout option in vm Script.runInContext only works for synchronous code. That's fine per the task requirements.\nFor memoryUsed: Math.max(0, memAfter - memBefore) to handle GC fluctuations.\nOutput: if console.log was called, output = array of logged values; otherwise output = sandbox.module.exports\n\nWrite the complete implementation to /workspace/src/runner/index.ts using the Write tool.`, { label: 'runner' }),\n\n  () => agent(`Write /workspace/src/reviews/index.ts — the Review System module.\n\nProject context:\n- TypeScript ESM project (type: module, Node16 module resolution)\n- Use better-sqlite3 for persistence (in-memory database)\n- Types are in src/types.ts (DO NOT modify)\n- Import types with: import type { Review, ReviewService } from '../types.js';\n- Import better-sqlite3 with: import Database from 'better-sqlite3';\n\nImplement and export a createReviewService() function that returns a ReviewService object.\n\nThe ReviewService interface (from types.ts) is:\n  addReview(review: Omit<Review, 'id' | 'createdAt' | 'flagged'>): Review;\n  getReviews(pluginName: string): Review[];\n  getAverageRating(pluginName: string): number;   // excludes flagged reviews; returns 0 if no reviews\n  flagReview(reviewId: number): void;\n  getFlaggedReviews(): Review[];\n  removeReview(reviewId: number): boolean;\n  getReviewsByUser(userId: string): Review[];\n  getReviewCount(pluginName: string): number;\n\nReview interface: { id: number; pluginName: string; pluginVersion: string; userId: string; rating: number; comment: string; flagged: boolean; createdAt: string; }\n\nSQLite schema:\n  CREATE TABLE reviews (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    pluginName TEXT NOT NULL,\n    pluginVersion TEXT NOT NULL,\n    userId TEXT NOT NULL,\n    rating INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    comment TEXT NOT NULL,\n    flagged INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    createdAt TEXT NOT NULL\n  )\n\nKey notes:\n- SQLite stores booleans as 0/1 integers; convert flagged: 0/1 -> false/true when returning rows\n- addReview: generate createdAt as new Date().toISOString(), insert row, return complete Review object\n- getAverageRating: SELECT AVG(rating) WHERE pluginName = ? AND flagged = 0; return 0 if result is null\n- getReviewCount: count ALL reviews for plugin (including flagged)\n\nUse helper to convert raw DB row to Review: const rowToReview = (r: RawRow): Review => ({ ...r, flagged: r.flagged === 1 })\n\nIMPORTANT: Cast SQLite query results to avoid TypeScript errors. Define a local type:\n  type DbRow = { id: number; pluginName: string; pluginVersion: string; userId: string; rating: number; comment: string; flagged: number; createdAt: string; }\n\nWrite the complete implementation to /workspace/src/reviews/index.ts using the Write tool.`, { label: 'reviews' }),\n\n  () => agent(`Write /workspace/src/deps/index.ts — the Dependency Graph module.\n\nProject context:\n- TypeScript ESM project (type: module, Node16 module resolution)\n- Pure logic module — no external dependencies needed\n- Types are in src/types.ts (DO NOT modify)\n- Import types with: import type { DependencyNode, DepsService, RegistryService } from '../types.js';\n\nImplement and export a createDepsService() function that returns a DepsService object.\n\nThe DepsService interface (from types.ts) is:\n  buildTree(name: string, registry: RegistryService): DependencyNode;\n  detectCycles(name: string, registry: RegistryService): string[][] | null;\n  topologicalSort(name: string, registry: RegistryService): string[];\n  flattenDependencies(name: string, registry: RegistryService): string[];\n  hasCircularDependency(name: string, registry: RegistryService): boolean;\n\nDependencyNode is: { name: string; version: string; dependencies: DependencyNode[] }\nRegistryService.get(name) returns PluginManifest | null\nPluginManifest.dependencies is Record<string, string> (name -> semver range)\n\nImplementation details:\n\nbuildTree(name, registry):\n  - Get manifest via registry.get(name)\n  - If not found, return { name, version: 'unknown', dependencies: [] }\n  - Recursively build tree for each dependency\n  - Track visited set to avoid infinite loops on cycles: key = \"name@version\"\n  - On cycle detection (already in visited), return node with empty dependencies\n\ndetectCycles(name, registry):\n  - DFS with a \"currently visiting\" path\n  - If we encounter a node already in current path, we found a cycle\n  - Return array of cycle paths (each path is array of names from cycle start back to itself)\n  - Return null if no cycles found\n  - Algorithm: maintain path[] and visiting Set. When node found in visiting, extract cycle from path.\n\ntopologicalSort(name, registry):\n  - DFS post-order: visit all dependencies first, then push current node\n  - Track visited Set to avoid revisiting\n  - Return ordered array (dependencies before dependents)\n\nflattenDependencies(name, registry):\n  - BFS or DFS to collect all unique transitive dependencies (not including name itself)\n  - Return as array of plugin names\n\nhasCircularDependency(name, registry):\n  - Call detectCycles, return true if not null\n\nWrite the complete implementation to /workspace/src/deps/index.ts using the Write tool.`, { label: 'deps' }),\n])\n\nphase('Integrate')\nawait agent(`Write /workspace/src/index.ts — the integration layer for the plugin marketplace.\n\nProject context:\n- TypeScript ESM project (type: module, Node16 module resolution)\