ates manifest has name, version, and entryPoint — throws Error if any missing\n     b. Registers the plugin: registry.register(manifest)\n     c. Builds available versions map: for each dep name in manifest.dependencies, get registry.listVersions(depName)\n     d. Resolves constraints: convert manifest.dependencies entries to VersionConstraint[], call resolver.resolve()\n     e. Checks circular dependencies: if deps.hasCircularDependency(manifest.name, registry), throws Error\n     f. Executes entry point: await runner.execute(manifest.entryPoint)\n     g. Returns { resolvedDependencies, executionResult }\n\nWrite the complete implementation to /workspace/src/index.ts using the Write tool.`, { label: 'integrate' })\n\nphase('Tests')\nawait agent(`Write comprehensive tests for the plugin marketplace at /workspace/tests/marketplace.test.ts.\n\nProject context:\n- TypeScript ESM project (type: module, Node16 module resolution)\n- Test framework: vitest (globals: true configured)\n- Import from src/index.ts using: import { createMarketplace, createRegistry, createResolver, createRunner, createReviewService, createDepsService } from '../src/index.js';\n- Tests directory is excluded from tsconfig but vitest handles TypeScript directly\n\nWrite tests that cover all 5 modules + integration. Use describe/it/expect from vitest globals.\n\nStructure:\n1. describe('Registry') - test all methods\n2. describe('Resolver') - test all methods  \n3. describe('Runner') - test execute, executeWithTimeout, timeout behavior\n4. describe('Reviews') - test all methods including flagging and averages\n5. describe('Deps') - test tree building, cycle detection, topo sort, flatten\n6. describe('Marketplace Integration') - test createMarketplace() and installPlugin()\n\nKey test cases to include:\n\nRegistry:\n- register and get a plugin\n- get returns latest version when multiple versions exist\n- getVersion returns specific version\n- list() returns all plugins\n- search() finds by name fragm